From: CB1 independent native transport work
Subject: [PATCH] R580 Pascal commit-coupled HDR10+ and strict native 422-10

Original implementation against NVIDIA 580.178.04 native modeset/KAPI and
Linux 7.2.6 shared HDR10PLUS_METADATA contract. No Hades source, patch,
helper, comment or test was read, copied, translated or imported here.
Public proprietary NvKmsFlip/RM/userspace layouts remain unchanged; only
kernel-client envelopes and the matched private KAPI grow.

Experimental commit-coupled packet programming, not hardware-FID certified.
Requires a primary atomic transaction, ready render fences, no outstanding
presentation, native HDMI, PQ/BT2020 and final native Pascal 422-10. Native
slot conflicts and unsupported topology are rejected. Runtime packet faults
are visible and retain ownership until a successful clear. Device boot and
physical HDMI packet/frame association remain unqualified.

